=== CELL 1: RABADON_MODE=silent (environment layer) ===
  $ rabadon status
    rabadon: SILENT — dormant everywhere, records nothing (`rabadon off` to watch again)
      read from: RABADON_MODE (environment variable)
    GATE EXIT=0  BYTES=0
  $ rabadon off      <- the command the screen itself printed
    rabadon: SILENT — dormant everywhere, records nothing (`rabadon off` to watch again)
  after running it, the SAME event through the SAME binary:
    GATE EXIT=0  BYTES=0

=== CELL 2: <proj>/.rabadon/mode = silent (project layer) ===
  $ rabadon status
    rabadon: SILENT — dormant everywhere, records nothing (`rabadon off` to watch again)
      read from: /tmp/f1e-c5.Nuc43A/proj/.rabadon/mode (present)
    GATE EXIT=0  BYTES=0
  $ rabadon off      <- the command the screen itself printed
    rabadon: SILENT — dormant everywhere, records nothing (`rabadon off` to watch again)
  after running it, the SAME event through the SAME binary:
    GATE EXIT=0  BYTES=0

=== CELL 3: <RABADON_DIR>/mode = silent (machine layer, control) ===
    rabadon: SILENT — dormant everywhere, records nothing (`rabadon off` to watch again)
      read from: /tmp/f1e-c5.W7J1FV/rdir/mode (present)
    GATE EXIT=0  BYTES=0
    rabadon: WATCH — recording what it WOULD have caught, touching nothing (`rabadon on` to act)
    GATE EXIT=0  BYTES=296

=== matrix coverage of the existing lock ===
  grep -c RABADON_MODE status_truth_test.sh = 0
  grep -c silent status_truth_test.sh = 7
